From 9c4078c49ccef3f36d6e25177033823e73d10d03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:31:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 64/65] RDoom 1.1.2: no running out of memory in long Project
 Brutality sessions

Console (PB + WadFusion, Legacy of Rust MAP08, ~11 minutes): "Could not
realloc 24263712 bytes". Every sprite, gore and weapon frame ever drawn kept
its GPU copy for the rest of the map, and each map start also loaded the
whole texture warm list, which had grown to 2000 pictures over four sessions.

- Texture eviction: every 5 s, with the heap above rd_vk_texevict_mb (2300 MB),
  sprite, decal and HUD pictures not drawn for 30 s (5 s above +400 MB) lose
  their GPU copy at the start of a frame, after the decode queue is flushed
  and the GPU is idle; all texture descriptor sets are rebuilt on next use.
  At most one pass per 30 s unless urgent. Ryujinx: 2-4 ms per pass.
- Warm list in order of use (most recent last, oldest dropped past 2000) and a
  warm-up budget (rd_vk_texwarm_mb, 256 MB, newest first; none above 1.8 GB).
- perf.log has the heap in use every 5 s; out-of-memory errors name the
  caller and the memory in use.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
